<section class="section section--hero">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <h1 class="display">The oldest call to prayer</h1>
    <p class="section-p">Before clocks and telephones, the church bell kept the hours and called the faithful to worship. Across America many towers have fallen silent. The foundation exists to help them ring again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap grid grid--story">
    <div class="stack prose">
      {#- The "For centuries the church bell..." paragraph left on 2026-10-16 (client: it repeats
          Home's Why we ring). The certification and filed-purpose sentences left on 2026-09-29
          (client: no legal-sounding wording; copy is being edited separately). #}
      <p class="section-p">This is a serious undertaking, not a pastime. The foundation supports the work of ringing: bells and their towers, pipe organs, rose windows and stained glass, and the training of the artisans who keep them.</p>
      <p class="section-p">There is more in a bell than announcement. Cast bronze rings at frequencies long associated with healing, a sound that brings calm to a street, a room, and the people in them. The foundation also makes grants to those who work with sound, color, and frequency for healing.</p>
    </div>
